# RESEED (hand-harvest, local on fix/retirement, forward-only): the §16 SYSCALL INTRINSIC keystone —
# raw OS syscalls as a codegen intrinsic (the post-pivot §16 foundation: libc is OUT, the target is the OS's
# native syscall/ABI, the way Go/Rust/Zig reach the kernel without a C compiler). What this harvest carries:
#   - **§16 syscall intrinsic (compiler — checker + codegen)**: `teko::sys::syscall0`..`syscall6(nr, a0..aN:
#     i64): i64` as compiler builtins (no `.tks` body, exactly like `f64_bits`). Args are `i64` register words
#     (ptr/uptr cannot cast to i64 — `cast_check` forbids it); the return is a raw `i64` (a negative value is
#     `-errno`; typed `Result` wrappers are ordinary `.tks` built on top).
#     - Checker: seven `syscallN` builtins registered next to `f64_bits` (`scope.tks`), admitted at any
#       `teko::sys::` qualifier depth by the existing `builtin_qualifier_ok`.
#     - Codegen: seven dispatch arms (`last == "syscallN"` → `tk_syscallN(...)`) next to `f64_bits`. The
#       lowering emits `static inline long tk_syscallN(...)` PREAMBLE helpers carrying `asm volatile("syscall"
#       ...)` with the x86_64 register convention (`rax`=nr+ret, args `rdi rsi rdx r10 r8 r9`, clobber `rcx r11
#       memory`), wrapped in `#if defined(__x86_64__)` / `#error` (aarch64 designed-ahead). The helpers are
#       USE-GATED by a `cg_scan_syscall_arities` pre-scan (mirroring the `cg_lift_*` recursion) so only arities
#       actually called are emitted — the C-leg intrinsic, exactly like the `f64_bits` intrinsic decision (no
#       runtime symbol, no libc). `teko::sys` gained the `SYS_EXIT_GROUP` x86_64(231)/aarch64(94) number pair,
#       `#os("linux") #arch(...)`-guarded.
#
# NOT INERT IN SOURCE, BUT NO BEHAVIORAL CORPUS DIVERGENCE. The compiler's own corpus (`src/`) issues ZERO
# syscalls, so the use-gated pre-scan emits NO `tk_syscallN` helper into the self-image; the emitted C differs
